    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the only one in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a per-day create-owner cap on `POST /api/owners`: once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`, the request is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md (mirroring the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` city-cap rule), I added:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws `OwnerDailyLimitException` at `DAILY_LIMIT = 100`. Runs before the owner is saved, so the count reflects only existing owners.\n- **`OwnerDailyLimitException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`OwnerDailyLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with the message body.\n- **Escalation YAML** `escalation/\u2026OwnerDailyLimitException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n- Inserted a `dailyLimit` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into `owners.POST.yml`, between address normalization and the uniqueness checks.",
